From ca527c68692c3ed8e2dd33d2b3a908a755bc9895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:00:17 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 page theme colour: theme-color events and a
 top-edge snapshot for the host's toolbar

Arc draws its toolbar strip in the page's colour: the page's
<meta name="theme-color">, else the colour along its top edge (PAN Home
declares none and gets its black top bar). The host had neither.

ABI 1.51 page_theme_color. ReArcEngineSetThemeColorCallback delivers
ReArcThemeColorEvent {document, has_color, argb} from the tab's services
observer (WebContents::GetThemeColor, DidChangeThemeColor): once when the
services attach, on each change, and once per new document so the host can
key it by document; an unchanged colour is not repeated. ReArcTabGetThemeColor
reads it. ReArcTabCaptureSnapshot scope 2 captures the visible viewport's top
4 CSS px at its scroll offset (a sticky header after a scroll), through the
same internal Page.captureScreenshot path as scope 0; the PNG is a few rows
(1600x8, 466 bytes, for an 800 pt viewport at 2x). No earlier struct
changed. Bridge 0.54.0.

Last rebased: 2026-11-08 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
